						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 2: MULTIPLE INSTANCES\n\nIn this example the Perlin Generator is used to randomly move multiple Circles.\nNote that the phase offset of each Perlin Generator is set to multiple.\nSelecting the node and inspecting the node panel shows us that each phase offset is unique.\nAlso note that, in the node panel, you can randomize the phase offset using the \"shuffle\" button in the multi-editor."
